{
  "$Comment": [
    "Reaching into the ground for a boulder and tearing it out. 78 frames at 60fps, so 1.3 seconds.",
    "Only the spine is animated. Foot IK replants the legs every tick whatever this says, and hand IK drives the digging arm to its goal, so the two arm tracks here are the counterweight the other arm swings out behind. Whichever arm the throw picks overrides its own track.",
    "Rotations are about the bone's X axis unless stated. Negative pitches the top of the body forward, which is why the crouch is negative and the rear back at the end is positive."
  ],
